<title>SPAIN: New BCH indicator sees Spain in EMU launch.</title>
<headline>New BCH indicator sees Spain in EMU launch.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial markets are discounting more than an 80 percent chance that Spain will join the launch of European Economic and Monetary Union (EMU) in 1999, according to a new indicator from Spain's Banco Central Hispano.</p>
<p>According to the &quot;Euro thermometre&quot;, the markets on Friday assigned a 82.56 percent chance to Spain entering EMU at its outset.</p>
<p>The indicator is based on the fixed portion of swaps rates.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
